,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nǁng language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nǁng_language,"Nǁng or Nǁŋǃke is an almost extinct Tuu language spoken in South Africa. It is commonly known by the ambiguous name of its only spoken dialect Nǀuu; the ǀʼAuni name for the Nǀuu, ǂKhomani, is used by the South African government.",Nǁng,Tuu
1,Nǁng — Wikipédia,https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nǁng,"Le nǁng ou nǀu est la seule langue survivante de la branche ǃkwi des langues tuu. Le dialecte nǀu, un des trois dialectes dont le noms est parfois utilisé pour désigner la langue et ses variantes, fait l'objet d'une campagne de préservation.Nǁng, sur Wikisource.",Nǁng,Tuu
2,Nǁng language,https://grokipedia.com/page/Nǁng_language,"Nǁng occupies a position within the !Ui branch of the Tuu language family, a genetic grouping of non-Khoe Khoisan languages historically labeled ""Southern Bushman"" by Dorothea Bleek in her 1929 comparative study.",Nǁng,Tuu
3,Nǁng – Endangered Voices Initiative,https://endangeredvoices.org/nǁng/,"Nǁng or Nǁŋǃke, which is also known as Nǀu, is the only surviving member of the !Ui branch of the Tuu language family. It was declared extinct in 1973, but in the 1990s the South African San Institute managed to find 25 people who could speak or understand the language.",Nǁng,Tuu
4,Nǁng | Polyglot Wiki | Fandom,https://speaky.fandom.com/wiki/Nǁng,"Nǁng, also known by the name Nǀuu, which is its only living dialect, is one of the two surviving Tuu Languages. It now only has one native speaker in South Africa.",Nǁng,Tuu
5,"Language Watch 4: Nǁng, Kalahari Desert",https://go.proz.com/blog/language-watch-nllng-kalahari,"Nǁng is one of the indigenous languages of South Africa, part of the Tuu language family found in parts of the interior, and in neighbouring Botswana. It’s spoken primarily by the San – the first tribe of hunter gatherers in the area, also known as “Bushmen”.",Nǁng,Tuu
6,ethnologue.com/language/ngh,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ngh/,Nǁng.,Nǁng,Tuu
7,Microsoft Word - 2014 03 Cape Town Nng,https://www.iaaw.hu-berlin.de/de/afrika/linguistik/mitarbeiter/prof-dr-phil-tom-gueldemann/dokumente/2014-03-cape-town-nng-h/@@download/file/2014+03+Cape+Town+Nng+H.pdf,> for Nǁng doculect by Pabst as well as many other non-Nǁng Tuu varieties further north. > second component - same as in saa.si above. > first component - a more specific exonym for San encountered by all Khoekhoe speaking.,Nǁng,Tuu
8,List Of 10 Of The Strangest Languages In The World,https://coursesdata.com/language-diversity/list-of-10-of-the-strangest-languages-in-the-world/,"9. Nǁng – The Endangered Click Language. Nǁng is a Tuu language from South Africa. Like Taa, it uses clicks, but it is even more endangered, with only a handful of elderly speakers remaining.",Nǁng,Tuu
9,muse.jhu.edu/article/683124,https://muse.jhu.edu/article/683124,"""Casting a Wider Net over Nǁng: The Older Archival Resources"".",Nǁng,Tuu
